---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="SMS Terms & Privacy | Chiropractic Grit"
  description="SMS messaging terms and privacy for messages sent by Chiropractic Grit to its users (chiropractors and practice staff) about waitlist, onboarding, billing, and platform notifications."
>
  <Nav />

  <main class="page">
    <div class="container">

      <!-- Header -->
      <div class="page-header">
        <div class="kicker">SMS Program & Terms</div>
        <h1>SMS program & terms.</h1>
        <p class="header-copy">
          This page describes the Chiropractic Grit SMS program — sender, phone number,
          message types, frequency, cost, opt-in and opt-out — and the legal terms
          governing its use.
        </p>
        <p class="last-updated">Last updated: May 8, 2026</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Content -->
      <div class="legal-content">

        <section>
          <h2>1. Sender</h2>
          <p>
            Messages on this program are sent by <strong>Chiropractic Grit LLC</strong>
            (operator of the Chiropractic Grit practice management platform at
            chiropracticgrit.com) from the number <strong>(719) 654-1843</strong>. Save
            this number to your contacts as "Chiropractic Grit" so messages are easy to
            recognize.
          </p>
          <p>
            Messages on this program are sent directly to Chiropractic Grit's prospective
            and active users — chiropractors and practice staff who have opted in. They
            are <strong>not</strong> sent on behalf of any chiropractic practice to any
            patient (see section 10).
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>2. What you'll receive</h2>
          <p>When you opt in, you may receive:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Waitlist updates and early-access invitations</li>
            <li>Onboarding and account-setup instructions</li>
            <li>Trial-status, billing, and subscription notifications</li>
            <li>Platform status notices (downtime, campaign-registration updates, etc.)</li>
            <li>Two-factor authentication (2FA) verification codes when you log in (only if you've enabled 2FA in account settings)</li>
            <li>Replies to messages you send to Chiropractic Grit support</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>3. Message frequency</h2>
          <p>
            Frequency varies, typically up to four messages per month per recipient.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>4. Cost</h2>
          <p>
            <strong>Msg &amp; data rates may apply.</strong> Chiropractic Grit does not
            charge users for SMS messages, but your mobile carrier's standard messaging
            rates apply.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>5. How to opt in</h2>
          <p>You can opt in to the Chiropractic Grit SMS program in any of these ways:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Waitlist form</strong> — Check the SMS consent box on chiropracticgrit.com/waitlist</li>
            <li><strong>Account onboarding</strong> — Check the SMS consent box during practice onboarding inside the Chiropractic Grit application</li>
            <li><strong>Account settings</strong> — Enable SMS notifications in your account preferences</li>
            <li><strong>2FA setup</strong> — Enabling two-factor authentication in your account security settings authorizes Chiropractic Grit to send verification codes to the phone number on file</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Each opt-in is recorded with a timestamp, the consent method, and the phone
            number you provided. We will not send you messages on this program through
            any other channel.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>6. How to opt out (STOP)</h2>
          <p>You can stop receiving SMS messages at any time by:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Replying <strong>STOP</strong> to any message from <strong>(719) 654-1843</strong></li>
            <li>Replying STOPALL, UNSUBSCRIBE, CANCEL, END, or QUIT — all are honored</li>
            <li>Disabling SMS in your account settings</li>
            <li>Emailing <a href="mailto:support@chiropracticgrit.com">support@chiropracticgrit.com</a> with the subject line "Opt out"</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            After you opt out, you will receive a single confirmation message and no
            further texts will be sent. You can opt back in at any time by re-enabling
            SMS notifications in your account or contacting support.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>7. Help (HELP)</h2>
          <p>
            Reply <strong>HELP</strong> to any message from <strong>(719) 654-1843</strong>
            for assistance, or email
            <a href="mailto:support@chiropracticgrit.com">support@chiropracticgrit.com</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>8. Privacy</h2>
          <p>
            Your phone number is stored securely and used only for the SMS message
            categories described in section 2. Chiropractic Grit will <strong>not</strong>
            sell, rent, or share your phone number with third parties for marketing
            purposes.
          </p>
          <p>
            SMS messages are delivered by Telnyx under a data-protection agreement that
            prohibits any use of your number outside of message delivery.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>9. Supported carriers</h2>
          <p>
            SMS messaging is supported on all major US carriers including AT&T, T-Mobile,
            and Verizon, as well as most regional carriers. Carriers are not liable for
            delayed or undelivered messages.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>10. Practice-to-patient SMS (future feature)</h2>
          <p>
            Patient-facing SMS sent by chiropractic practices through Grit is in
            development and is not currently active. When that capability ships, each
            practice will register its own SMS sender with the carriers under its own
            legal entity, collect its own patient consent, and become the sender of
            record for those messages. Separate terms governing patient consent, HIPAA
            content rules, and TCPA obligations will be presented to practices and
            patients at that time. Nothing in this document applies retroactively to
            that future program.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>11. Changes to these terms</h2>
          <p>
            We may update these terms from time to time. Changes will be reflected on
            this page with an updated date. Continued use of SMS services after changes
            constitutes acceptance of the revised terms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="contact-section">
          <h2>12. Contact</h2>
          <p>For questions about SMS messaging, privacy, or to request opt-out assistance, email <a href="mailto:support@chiropracticgrit.com">support@chiropracticgrit.com</a> or use any of the opt-out methods in section 6.</p>
        </section>

      </div>

    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page {
    padding: 52px 0 84px;
  }

  .page-header {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin-bottom: 52px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
  }

  .kicker {
    color: var(--ember);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 4.5vw, 3.6rem);
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .header-copy {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  .last-updated {
    color: var(--subtle);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .legal-content {
    max-width: 740px;
  }

  section {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
    padding-bottom: 40px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  section:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }

  p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.97rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }

  p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 10px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  li::before {
    content: '';
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--ember);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 8px;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--ember);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  a:hover {
    color: var(--ember-strong);
  }

  strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .page {
      padding: 36px 0 64px;
    }

    section {
      margin-bottom: 28px;
      padding-bottom: 28px;
    }
  }
</style>
